Z||000000||Formula 18||07-12-2000||11:02 AM||||OK Long Subject, I know. <BR>Here is the question, Is the 3.4L in the camaro's the same engine that is in the  Pontiac Transport's and Chevy APV's? I looked on the CArPoint site and it said the came with a 180 hp 3.4L block. Sounds good to me. You might not even have to switch the starter b/c it would be in the right place b/c it would come out of a FWD car. Anyone know if this would work?? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-12-2000||02:14 PM||||I belive the 3.4 minivan motor has aluminum heads and a completely different induction and ignition system. I suspect that it will bolt in, but will require the transplant of the entire ECM and harness (unless you're an electronics wizard. Probably then, too).<BR>Won't look like a stock 2.8, so you'll lose the "stealth" factor, as well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||07-12-2000||06:01 PM||||It seems I saw this addressed here, or maybe I read it someplace, but if I recall, the motors on the minvans were roller motors, with roller cams and rockers. I don't really recall all the details, but would be worth a search to find out.||||reg||1
